21": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Old", "64722924": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Old", "64722927": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Old", "64722930": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Old", "64722933": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Old", "64722936": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722939": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722942": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722945": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722948": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722951": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722954": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722957": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722960": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "64722963": "Figures 2, 4 and 5 PNNs quantification/Young", "68895760": ""}, "authors": [{"id": 22661912, "full_name": "Alejandra Gomez", "first_name": "Alejandra", "last_name": "Gomez", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Alejandra_Gomez", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 23928597, "full_name": "Aric Logsdon", "first_name": "Aric", "last_name": "Logsdon", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Aric_Logsdon", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 21589238, "full_name": "Jeremy Bailoo", "first_name": "Jeremy", "last_name": "Bailoo", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Jeremy_Bailoo", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 23486938, "full_name": "Gail Cornwall", "first_name": "Gail", "last_name": "Cornwall", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Gail_Cornwall", "orcid_id": "0000-0002-2903-1690"}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/Data_associated_with_manuscript_Altered_brain_extracellular_matrix_structure_and_sex-specific_learning_memory_dysfunction_in_mice_lacking_the_functional_amyloid_Cystatin-related_epididymal_spermatogenic_CRES_/31855621", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\">Cystatin-related epididymal spermatogenic (CRES) is a member of a reproductive subgroup of family 2 cystatins and part of a functional amyloid-containing extracellular matrix (ECM) with host defense functions in the epididymal lumen. CRES and the endogenous epididymal amyloid matrix exhibit high plasticity, forming distinct amyloid structures, with antimicrobial functions tailored to specific bacterial strains. We recently demonstrated that CRES/CRES amyloid is also present in the mammalian brain ECM. In this study, we utilized a CRES knockout (KO) mouse model to determine if the loss of CRES altered the structure of the hippocampal and cortical ECM and impacts brain function. We report that CRES KO male and female mice exhibited sex-specific structural changes in both the loose/interstitial and perineuronal net (PNN) ECM. Additionally, young CRES KO males\u2014but not females\u2014displayed deficits in learning, memory and executive functioning when compared to WT controls. In contrast, older CRES KO males did not exhibit behavioral deficits, a finding that correlated with the observation of a similar PNN ECM structure when compared to WT mice. Our data suggest that CRES functions as a regulatory or structural component of the brain ECM, contributing to its sex-specific structural organization and plasticity, affecting sex-specific behaviors of learning and memory.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 2, "status": "public", "size": 98733398, "created_date": "2026-09-18T15:54:35Z", "modified_date": "2026-09-18T15:54:36Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["hippocampus", "cerebral cortex", "mouse", "neuroplasticity", "cystatin", "Brain Extracellular Matrix", "functional amyloid", "CSPG"], "keywords": ["hippocampus", "cerebral cortex", "mouse", "neuroplasticity", "cystatin", "Brain Extracellular Matrix", "functional amyloid", "CSPG"], "categories": [{"id": 24154, "title": "Glycobiology", "parent_id": 24133, "path": "/24130/24133/24154", "source_id": "310107", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 24178, "title": "Biochemistry and cell biology not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 24133, "path": "/24130/24133/24178", "source_id": "310199", "taxonomy_id": 100}], "references": [], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "Gomez, Alejandra; Logsdon, Aric; Bailoo, Jeremy; Cornwall, Gail (2026). Data associated with manuscript \"Altered brain extracellular matrix structure and sex-specific learning/memory dysfunction in mice lacking the functional amyloid Cystatin-related epididymal spermatogenic (CRES).\". figshare. Dataset. https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.31855621.v2", "related_materials": [], "is_embargoed": false, "embargo_date": null, "embargo_type": null, "embargo_title": "", "embargo_reason": "", "embargo_options": [], "id": 31855621, "title": "Data associated with manuscript \"Altered brain extracellular matrix structure and sex-specific learning/memory dysfunction in mice lacking the functional amyloid Cystatin-related epididymal spermatogenic (CRES).\"", "doi": "10.6084/m9.figshare.31855621.v2", "handle": "", "url": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/31855621", "published_date": "2026-09-18T15:54:35Z", "thumb": "https://s3-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/pfigshare-u-previews/68895760/thumb.png", "defined_type": 3, "defined_type_name": "dataset", "group_id": null, "url_private_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/account/articles/31855621", "url_public_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/31855621", "url_private_html": "https://figshare.com/account/articles/31855621", "url_public_html": "https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/Data_associated_with_manuscript_Altered_brain_extracellular_matrix_structure_and_sex-specific_learning_memory_dysfunction_in_mice_lacking_the_functional_amyloid_Cystatin-related_epididymal_spermatogenic_CRES_/31855621", "timeline": {"posted": "2026-09-18T15:54:35"}, "reso